- **Error Handling:** Implement comprehensive error handling throughout the application to catch and manage exceptions effectively. This will help to identify root causes when encountering Internal Server Errors, instead of allowing the application to fail silently.

- **Template Rendering:** Verify that all templates are properly linked and that routes are correctly defined. Ensure that user roles and sessions are validated before rendering pages to determine which elements should be displayed.

- **Session Management:** Establish clear session management protocols to ensure users remain logged in across different pages and ensure necessary data is passed correctly between routes.

- **Modular Code Structure:** Develop a modular structure for the application to isolate functionality into manageable components. This includes separating user authentication, data handling, and rendering logic to simplify debugging and improve code maintainability.

- **Input Validation:** Incorporate strong input validation to safeguard against malformed data submissions in forms. This includes both client-side and server-side validation to ensure the application remains robust against unexpected user inputs.

- **Logging and Monitoring:** Set up logging and monitoring to track application behavior in real-time. This will help in diagnosing issues and generating informative outputs that can be analyzed to improve application reliability over time.

By focusing on these aspects, future development can become more resilient to errors and provide a smoother experience for users.|
